NEARS-1601 — task_bug: store_screen chips gain a SECOND focus stop (double-announce)
=====================================================================================
Device: emulator-5556 (448x997dp, density 480)   Surface: UserApp store_screen (Burger Palace)
Fix APK md5:  06395b9316fabc85e927810551587120  (worktree feat/NEARS-1601-nfilterchip-semantics @ 6e9c6c21)
Base APK md5: 2b9ffbb45025ac55f5051f34dde51231  (detached @ 38464d91, merge-base)
Oracle: `adb shell uiautomator dump` = the real Android AccessibilityNodeInfo tree a screen
reader consumes. Corroborated by Flutter `ext.flutter.debugDumpSemanticsTreeInTraversalOrder`.

WHY: UserApp/lib/features/store/screens/store_screen.dart wraps NFilterChip in its OWN
Semantics(button:true, selected:..., label:...) at lines 1682 and 1740 — a pre-1601
compensating workaround for the very gap 1601 fixes (its own comment says "an unwrapped chip
announced no selection state at all — silence, not 'not selected'"). It is the ONLY call site
that does this (verified by scanning all 29 NFilterChip call sites). Now that the element
publishes selection natively, the wrapper is redundant AND it no longer merges: the new
Semantics(selected:, button:) inserted between the wrapper and the InkWell splits what used to
be one node into two.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MERGE-BASE (pre-fix) — ONE focus stop per chip, label duplicated INSIDE the one node
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
content-desc='All\nAll'              selected=true  clickable=true  focusable=true
content-desc='Offers filter\nOffers' selected=false clickable=true  focusable=true
content-desc='Sides\nSides'          selected=false clickable=true  focusable=true
content-desc='Drinks\nDrinks'        selected=false clickable=true  focusable=true
content-desc='Pizza\nPizza'          selected=false clickable=true  focusable=true
content-desc='Burgers\nBurgers'      selected=false clickable=true  focusable=true

Flutter tree corroboration (base):
       │ │   │   flags: isButton, isFocusable, hasSelectedState
       │ │   │   label:
       │ │   │     "Sides
       │ │   │     Sides"

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FIX BUILD (post-1601) — TWO focus stops per chip, EACH carrying the selection state
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
content-desc='All'           selected=true  clickable=false focusable=true   <-- wrapper node
content-desc='All'           selected=true  clickable=true  focusable=true   <-- chip node
content-desc='Offers filter' selected=false clickable=false focusable=true
content-desc='Offers'        selected=false clickable=true  focusable=true
content-desc='Sides'         selected=false clickable=false focusable=true
content-desc='Sides'         selected=false clickable=true  focusable=true
content-desc='Drinks'        selected=false clickable=false focusable=true
content-desc='Drinks'        selected=false clickable=true  focusable=true
content-desc='Pizza'         selected=false clickable=false focusable=true
content-desc='Pizza'         selected=false clickable=true  focusable=true
content-desc='Burgers'       selected=false clickable=false focusable=true
content-desc='Burgers'       selected=false clickable=true  focusable=true

Flutter tree corroboration (fix), nested parent -> child:
         │   │ │ flags: isButton, hasSelectedState
         │   │ │ label: "Offers filter"
         │   │ └─SemanticsNode#1032
         │   │     flags: isButton, isFocusable, hasSelectedState
         │   │     label: "Offers"

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IMPACT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TalkBack focus stops on the store category rail go 6 -> 12; every chip announces its name and
its selection state twice ("Sides, not selected, button" ... "Sides, not selected, button").
Both builds are defective, but the axis the ticket exists to fix — say the state exactly once —
regresses here: state was published once pre-fix, twice post-fix.

CONFINED TO store_screen. All other NFilterChip surfaces observed live show exactly ONE node per
chip: cuisine_filter_row, category_screen, search_screen(history), store_item_search_screen,
all_store_filter_widget, all_store_screen, add_address_screen, item_bottom_sheet (both sites).

SUGGESTED FIX (engineer): delete the now-redundant Semantics(button:, selected:, label:)
wrappers at store_screen.dart:1682 and :1740 — the same cleanup 1601 already performed on
item_bottom_sheet's hand-wired state word. Not applied here: QA does not edit product code.

NOTE: the DLS unit suite (23/23 green, incl. 4 new NEARS-1601 tests) CANNOT catch this — it
exercises NFilterChip in isolation, never wrapped in a call site's own Semantics.
